Patch: 009-nested-tie-turn
Reason: the records of a nested call whose script could not be told named no turn, so a recovery listed such a call from an earlier turn under this turn's cut-off exec (telling the model its script made calls it never made); each record carries the turn it ran in and only the interrupted turn's are listed, once, apart, in the last cut-off exec's output, and the recovery note is injected as a developer message on a new thread as on a resumed one, so it is never in a user turn
Upstream: ours
Pins: code mode: an unwatched answer's call in an earlier turn is not listed by a later turn's recovery
Pins: recovery note: a crash before the rollout was mirrored (a new thread) still gets the note as a developer message, in no user message
